From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uri Shaked <uri@urishaked.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] bootloader: copy the kernel Image by 32-bit words by
 default

Every load, store and instruction fetch on the KianV SoC is its own
QSPI transaction, so the byte-by-byte copy of a 3.4 MB Image took 79 s
at 30 MHz on ttsky25a silicon. Copying words takes 22 s and brings the
shell prompt from about 209 s to about 151 s. WORD_COPY=0 restores the
old behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 asic/os/ulinux_asic_kianv_soc/bootloader/Makefile | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/asic/os/ulinux_asic_kianv_soc/bootloader/Makefile b/asic/os/ulinux_asic_kianv_soc/bootloader/Makefile
index 60b9195..f93dfc8 100644
--- a/asic/os/ulinux_asic_kianv_soc/bootloader/Makefile
+++ b/asic/os/ulinux_asic_kianv_soc/bootloader/Makefile
@@ -16,7 +16,10 @@ IMAGE_SIZE ?= $(shell wc -c < ../Image)
 endif
 SOC_HAS_SPI ?= 0
 XIP_KERNEL ?= 0
-WORD_COPY ?= 0
+# Copy the kernel Image 32 bits at a time (~3.6x faster than byte copy on
+# silicon: 22 s instead of 79 s for a 3.4 MB Image at 30 MHz). Set to 0 for
+# the original byte-by-byte copy.
+WORD_COPY ?= 1
 
 LDS_FILE ?= kianv.ld
 START_FILE = crt0.S
